{
  "id": "exclusion-rescue",
  "description": "The #44 targeted readmission. An exclusion pattern fired, but a replication phrase and a specific author-year cite are both present \u2014 the shape of an in-scope computational reproduction the exclusions misfire on ('replicated the analysis code of Smith (2019)'). Outranks the whole 500s band so the readmission wins, and lands in the cheap discard-only tier: the evidence is enough to refuse a terminal discard, not enough to buy the expensive screen. The cite clause is one RE2-safe approximation of an author-year citation (parenthetical, narrative and et-al forms); it replaces extract_author_year_patterns()'s lookahead-based patterns and its bare-name blacklist. Divergence 2 in docs/filter-engine.md: the cite only orders spend, it no longer admits, so an approximation is enough.",
